### Configure datafusion.runtime.memory_limit via SQL

Source: https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/main/docs/source/user-guide/configs.md

Use the SET command to define the maximum memory limit for query execution.

```sql
SET datafusion.runtime.memory_limit = '2G';
```

### Collect / Streaming Exec

Source: https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/main/docs/source/library-user-guide/using-the-dataframe-api.md

DataFusion DataFrames are lazy, meaning they defer processing until execution. This allows for optimizations. You can execute a DataFrame using `collect` to buffer all output into a `Vec<RecordBatch>`, `execute_stream` to get a `SendableRecordBatchStream` for incremental computation, or `cache` to buffer output into a new in-memory DataFrame.

--------------------------------

### Architecture > Memory Management

Source: https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/main/dev/changelog/51.0.0.md

A SpillingPool has been added to manage collections of spill files. This component is likely used for handling intermediate data that exceeds available memory during query execution.
